  <!-- CHAPTER ONE -->

  <section class="chapter" id="chapter-1">

    <div class="chapter-number">
      Chapter One
    </div>

    <h2>Before the Beginning</h2>

    <p>
      Before there were kingdoms, there were whispers.
    </p>

    <p>
      Before there were temples, there were stars.
    </p>

    <p>
      Before men carved the names of their gods into stone,
      there was a mystery older than memory itself.
    </p>

    <p>
      And before the first word was spoken upon the earth,
      something was already waiting.
    </p>

    <p>
      The night was silent.
    </p>

    <p>
      Not the ordinary silence of sleeping villages or empty
      deserts, but a silence so complete that it seemed the
      universe itself had stopped breathing.
    </p>

    <p>
      There was no moon.
    </p>

    <p>
      No sun.
    </p>

    <p>
      No wind moving through trees.
    </p>

    <p>
      No sea breaking against a shore.
    </p>

    <p>
      Only darkness.
    </p>

    <div class="scene-break">✦ ✦ ✦</div>

    <p>
      Then, somewhere beyond the boundaries of what would
      one day be called creation, a light appeared.
    </p>

    <p>
      It was not a flame.
      It did not burn.
      It did not cast shadows.
      It simply existed.
    </p>

    <p>
      And within that light stood a figure.
    </p>

    <p>
      He was neither old nor young. His face seemed to change
      whenever the darkness moved around him, as though time
      itself could not decide what he was supposed to look like.
    </p>

    <p>
      He looked into the emptiness.
    </p>

    <p>
      And the emptiness looked back.
    </p>

    <p>
      For an age beyond counting, nothing happened.
    </p>

    <p>
      Then the figure spoke.
    </p>

    <p>
      Not loudly.
      Not with anger.
      Not with force.
    </p>

    <p>
      His voice moved through the darkness like the first
      breath of existence.
    </p>

    <p>
      <em>“Let there be light.”</em>
    </p>

    <p>
      And the darkness remembered that it had never truly
      been empty.
    </p>

    <p>
      Something answered.
    </p>

    <p>
      A thousand distant lights awakened.
    </p>

    <p>
      Then a million.
    </p>

    <p>
      Then more than the mind of any future human being
      would ever be capable of counting.
    </p>

    <p>
      The heavens unfolded.
    </p>

    <p>
      Stars ignited across the infinite black.
    </p>

    <p>
      Worlds formed in silence.
    </p>

    <p>
      Dust became stone.
      Stone became mountains.
      Water gathered in places where there had never been oceans.
    </p>

    <div class="scene-break">✦ ✦ ✦</div>

    <p>
      And somewhere among the countless worlds, one small
      blue sphere began its long journey toward humanity.
    </p>

    <p>
      But the figure watched that world more closely than
      all the others.
    </p>

    <p>
      Because he knew what would happen there.
    </p>

    <p>
      He knew about the first cities.
      The first kings.
      The first wars.
      The first prayers.
    </p>

    <p>
      He knew about prophets who would wander through
      deserts carrying messages nobody wanted to hear.
    </p>

    <p>
      And he knew that one day, in a small land between
      empires, a child would be born.
    </p>

    <p>
      A child whose name would travel farther than the
      armies of kings.
    </p>

    <p>
      A child who would be called many things.
    </p>

    <p>
      Teacher.
      Prophet.
      Messiah.
      Son.
      Servant.
      Light.
    </p>

    <p>
      And by some, Yehoshua.
    </p>

    <p>
      But that birth was still far away.
    </p>

    <p>
      First came the beginning.
    </p>

    <p>
      And before the beginning, there was a secret.
    </p>

    <p>
      The secret was this:
    </p>

    <p>
      <strong>
        Humanity had never been abandoned.
      </strong>
    </p>

    <p>
      It had only forgotten how to listen.
    </p>

    <p>
      The figure turned toward the newborn world.
    </p>

    <p>
      For the first time, something resembling sorrow crossed
      his face.
    </p>

    <p>
      <em>“Soon,”</em> he whispered.
    </p>

    <p>
      Then the stars moved.
    </p>

    <p>
      And history began.
    </p>

  </section>


  <!-- FUTURE CHAPTERS -->

  <section class="chapter" id="chapter-2">

    <div class="chapter-number">Chapter Two</div>

    <h2>The Garden</h2>

    <p>
      The story of humanity had not yet begun.
      But the place where it would begin was already being prepared.
    </p>

    <p>
      Far below the heavens, rivers gathered beneath a sky
      untouched by smoke, war, or the footsteps of kings.
    </p>

    <p>
      Something was coming.
    </p>

  </section>


  <section class="chapter" id="chapter-3">

    <div class="chapter-number">Chapter Three</div>

    <h2>The First Breath</h2>

    <p>
      The earth was silent when the first man opened his eyes.
    </p>

    <p>
      He did not know his name.
      He did not know the names of the stars.
      He did not know fear.
    </p>

    <p>
      He knew only that he was alive.
    </p>

  </section>


  <section class="chapter" id="chapter-4">

    <div class="chapter-number">Chapter Four</div>

    <h2>The Watchers</h2>

    <p>
      Above the mountains, something watched.
    </p>

    <p>
      They had watched humanity since the first breath.
      Some were guardians.
      Others had begun to wonder whether the laws of heaven
      were meant to be broken.
    </p>

  </section>


  <section class="chapter" id="chapter-5">

    <div class="chapter-number">Chapter Five</div>

    <h2>The Hidden Name</h2>

    <p>
      Generations would pass before the name Yehoshua was
      spoken beneath the stars.
    </p>

    <p>
      But the name already existed in the mystery waiting
      at the beginning.
    </p>

  </section>


  <!-- NAVIGATION -->

  <div class="reader-navigation">

    <button onclick="window.scrollTo({top:0, behavior:'smooth'})">
      ↑ Beginning
    </button>

    <button onclick="nextChapter()">
      Next Chapter →
    </button>

  </div>

  <div class="page-counter">
    Book One · Before the Beginning
  </div>

</main>


<script>

  function toggleMenu() {
    document
      .getElementById("chapterMenu")
      .classList.toggle("open");
  }


  /* READING PROGRESS */

  window.addEventListener("scroll", function () {

    const scrollTop =
      document.documentElement.scrollTop ||
      document.body.scrollTop;

    const scrollHeight =
      document.documentElement.scrollHeight -
      document.documentElement.clientHeight;

    const progress =
      (scrollTop / scrollHeight) * 100;

    document.getElementById("progressBar").style.width =
      progress + "%";

  });


  /* NEXT CHAPTER */

  function nextChapter() {

    const chapters =
      document.querySelectorAll(".chapter");

    const current =
      window.scrollY;

    for (let i = 0; i < chapters.length; i++) {

      if (chapters[i].offsetTop > current + 100) {

        chapters[i].scrollIntoView({
          behavior: "smooth"
        });

        break;
      }

    }

  }

</script>

