  <h1>THE AWAKENED</h1>

  <h2>Book One: Before the Beginning</h2>

  <div class="chapter">
    Chapter One
  </div>

  <div class="chapter-title">
    The First Breath
  </div>

  <p>
    Adam stood beneath the trees and listened.
  </p>

  <p>
    He did not yet understand the sound of his own breathing.
    Each breath seemed to surprise him.
  </p>

  <p>
    He lifted his hands and turned them slowly beneath the
    light. He opened and closed his fingers, studying them as
    though they belonged to someone else.
  </p>

  <p>
    He touched the ground.
  </p>

  <p>
    It was warm.
  </p>

  <p>
    He touched the bark of a tree.
  </p>

  <p>
    Rough.
  </p>

  <p>
    He placed his palm against the surface of the water.
  </p>

  <p>
    The reflection looking back at him was the first human
    face he had ever seen.
  </p>

  <p>
    Adam stared.
  </p>

  <p>
    The image stared back.
  </p>

  <p>
    He smiled.
  </p>

  <p>
    The reflection smiled.
  </p>

  <p>
    For a moment, Adam laughed.
  </p>

  <p>
    It was the first human laughter.
  </p>

  <div class="scene-break">
    ✦ ✦ ✦
  </div>

  <p>
    Then he heard the voice again.
  </p>

  <p>
    “Adam.”
  </p>

  <p>
    He turned.
  </p>

  <p>
    There was no one standing behind him.
  </p>

  <p>
    “Adam.”
  </p>

  <p>
    This time the voice seemed to come from everywhere.
  </p>

  <p>
    From the trees.
  </p>

  <p>
    From the river.
  </p>

  <p>
    From the wind moving through the leaves.
  </p>

  <p>
    But most strangely, Adam felt that the voice was also
    coming from somewhere inside him.
  </p>

  <p>
    “I am here,” Adam answered.
  </p>

  <p>
    The words surprised him.
  </p>

  <p>
    He had spoken.
  </p>

  <p>
    Language had entered the world.
  </p>

  <p>
    The Creator answered:
  </p>

  <p>
    “You are alive.”
  </p>

  <p>
    Adam looked toward the sky.
  </p>

  <p>
    “What am I?”
  </p>

  <p>
    There was silence.
  </p>

  <p>
    Then came the answer.
  </p>

  <p>
    “You are human.”
  </p>

  <p>
    Adam repeated the word quietly.
  </p>

  <p>
    “Human.”
  </p>

  <p>
    He did not understand its full meaning.
  </p>

  <p>
    But he knew it belonged to him.
  </p>

  <p>
    “Why am I here?”
  </p>

  <p>
    The answer did not come immediately.
  </p>

  <p>
    Instead, the wind moved through the garden.
  </p>

  <p>
    Leaves danced above him.
  </p>

  <p>
    Birds crossed the sky.
  </p>

  <p>
    Adam watched them disappear beyond the trees.
  </p>

  <p>
    Then the Creator said:
  </p>

  <p>
    “To live.”
  </p>

  <p>
    Adam waited.
  </p>

  <p>
    “To learn.”
  </p>

  <p>
    He waited again.
  </p>

  <p>
    “To choose.”
  </p>

  <p>
    Adam looked toward the center of the garden.
  </p>

  <p>
    He could see the two mysterious trees standing in the
    distance.
  </p>

  <p>
    Something about them drew his attention.
  </p>

  <p>
    “What are those?”
  </p>

  <p>
    The silence that followed was different from the silence
    before.
  </p>

  <p>
    Adam felt it.
  </p>

  <p>
    Something important was being withheld.
  </p>

  <p>
    Finally, the Creator spoke.
  </p>

  <p>
    “They are part of the garden.”
  </p>

  <p>
    Adam looked at them again.
  </p>

  <p>
    “May I touch them?”
  </p>

  <p>
    “One you may know.”
  </p>

  <p>
    Adam waited for the rest.
  </p>

  <p>
    “And the other?”
  </p>

  <p>
    “The other must wait.”
  </p>

  <div class="scene-break">
    ✦ ✦ ✦
  </div>

  <p>
    High above the garden, the Watchers listened.
  </p>

  <p>
    One of them stepped forward.
  </p>

  <p>
    His name had not yet been spoken by human lips.
  </p>

  <p>
    But among the heavenly beings, he was known as Azar.
  </p>

  <p>
    He looked down upon Adam.
  </p>

  <p>
    “He does not understand,” Azar said.
  </p>

  <p>
    Another Watcher answered:
  </p>

  <p>
    “He was not created knowing everything.”
  </p>

  <p>
    “Then he is vulnerable.”
  </p>

  <p>
    “So are we.”
  </p>

  <p>
    Azar turned sharply.
  </p>

  <p>
    “We are not like him.”
  </p>

  <p>
    The other Watcher looked toward the garden.
  </p>

  <p>
    “Perhaps not.”
  </p>

  <p>
    “Then why does the Creator watch him so closely?”
  </p>

  <p>
    No answer came.
  </p>

  <p>
    Below them, Adam continued walking.
  </p>

  <p>
    He touched flowers.
  </p>

  <p>
    He listened to birds.
  </p>

  <p>
    He watched animals move through the grass.
  </p>

  <p>
    He gave names to the things he encountered.
  </p>

  <p>
    Lion.
  </p>

  <p>
    Eagle.
  </p>

  <p>
    Serpent.
  </p>

  <p>
    Deer.
  </p>

  <p>
    Tree.
  </p>

  <p>
    River.
  </p>

  <p>
    Sky.
  </p>

  <p>
    Each name became part of the world.
  </p>

  <p>
    But as the day passed, Adam began to notice something.
  </p>

  <p>
    Every creature had another like itself.
  </p>

  <p>
    Every bird had another bird.
  </p>

  <p>
    Every deer had another deer.
  </p>

  <p>
    Every creature seemed to belong to something.
  </p>

  <p>
    Adam looked around.
  </p>

  <p>
    And for the first time since opening his eyes,
    he felt something he could not name.
  </p>

  <p>
    Loneliness.
  </p>

  <p>
    He sat beside the river.
  </p>

  <p>
    The sun began to fall toward the horizon.
  </p>

  <p>
    Adam watched the light disappear.
  </p>

  <p>
    And somewhere beyond the garden, the Creator already
    knew what would happen next.
  </p>

  <p>
    Adam closed his eyes.
  </p>

  <p>
    Then the earth beneath him began to tremble.
  </p>

  <p>
    Not violently.
  </p>

  <p>
    Gently.
  </p>

  <p>
    Like a heartbeat.
  </p>

  <p>
    Adam opened his eyes.
  </p>

  <p>
    A strange light appeared beside him.
  </p>

  <p>
    He stood.
  </p>

  <p>
    And within that light, another form began to emerge.
  </p>

  <p>
    Adam stared.
  </p>

  <p>
    For the first time, he was no longer alone.
  </p>

  <div class="scene-break">
    ✦ ✦ ✦
  </div>

  <p>
    The Watchers looked down in silence.
  </p>

  <p>
    And Azar whispered:
  </p>

  <p>
    “Now the story truly begins.”
  </p>

